<title>UK: Independent forecasts for UK inflation edge higher.</title>
<headline>Independent forecasts for UK inflation edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent forecasts for underlying 1996 UK retail price inflation edged up to 2.7 percent in October from 2.6 percent in the previous two months, according to the latest summary of independent forecasts compiled by the Treasury.</p>
<p>Inflation forecasts for 1997 from independent and City institutions also edged higher, while GDP estimates for 1996 averaged 2.3 percent in October compared with 2.2 percent in September.</p>
<p>Following are key forecasts from the Treasury compilation (annual percentage changes unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>    AVERAGE OF NEW FORECASTS	     1996	 1997</p>
<p>    GDP					   2.3	  3.3</p>
<p>    RPI (Q4)				    2.2	  3.5</p>
<p>    RPIX (Q4)				   2.7	  2.9</p>
<p>    Unemployment (Q4, millions)	   2.08	 1.90</p>
<p>    Current account deficit (bln stg)   2.2	  5.6</p>
<p>    PSBR (bln stg)			   28.0	 23.5</p>
<p>    Interest rates (Q4)		     5.78	 6.99</p>
<p>NOTE: RPI is retail price index. RPIX is retail price index excluding mortgage interest payments (underlying inflation). PSBR is public sector borrowing requirement (budget deficit) and estimates are for the financial year to April 5</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
